meta {
  name: Verify Email
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email?userId={{userId}}&token={{verificationToken}}
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Manual verification flow:
  1. Register a user via 01_register.bru - note the returned user id and set it as {{userId}}.
  2. The registration handler emails a 6-character verification code via UserRegisteredDomainEventHandler.
     In dev without Mailtrap credentials configured, EmailService logs a warning and skips sending -
     check the Identity.API console/logs, or read the code directly from Redis: `evt:{userId}:{token}`.
  3. Set {{verificationToken}} to that code and send this request.
  4. Confirm success by calling GET /api/auth/me/verification-status (bearer auth) or 03_get_me.bru,
     which should now show isVerified/isEmailVerified as true.
}
